<div class="hero">
  <div class="hero__content">
    <p class="text-sm text-muted text-uppercase">Simple Web Deployment</p>
    <h1 class="hero__title">Deploy Your Website Without Managing the Server</h1>
    <p class="hero__subtitle">
      HelloDeploy gives you a guided way to publish and manage supported web applications
      without configuring every part of a server yourself. Configure your project, deploy it,
      connect a domain, manage environment variables, read the logs, and publish updates from
      one place.
    </p>
    <div class="button-group mt-6">
      <a href="/auth/create-account" class="button button--primary button--lg">Deploy a Project</a>
      <a href="/how-it-works" class="button button--secondary button--lg">See How It Works</a>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-4">
      Built for developers, students, freelancers, educators, and small teams.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card__body text-center">
    <h2 class="feature-title">A simpler path from code to a live website</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">
      Deploying an application usually means more than uploading files. Depending on the
      project you may need to install dependencies, run a build, set a start command, define
      environment variables, expose the right port, connect a domain, and read the logs when
      something fails. HelloDeploy brings those steps into one workflow.
    </p>
    <ol class="flow mt-6">
      <li class="flow__step">Project</li>
      <li class="flow__step">Configure</li>
      <li class="flow__step">Build</li>
      <li class="flow__step">Deploy</li>
      <li class="flow__step">Connect a domain</li>
      <li class="flow__step">Go live</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="button-group mt-6">
      <a href="/how-it-works" class="button button--secondary">Learn How Deployment Works</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2 class="feature-title mt-8 text-center">Everything you need to manage a deployment</h2>

<div class="feature-grid mt-4">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__body">
      <p class="feature-icon"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'repository' }) %></p>
      <h3 class="feature-title">Guided deployment</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Connect a repository. HelloDeploy inspects it, proposes build and start settings, and
        tells you what it had to assume.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__body">
      <p class="feature-icon"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'activity' }) %></p>
      <h3 class="feature-title">Deployment logs</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Follow a deployment as it runs, and see which stage failed when one does.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__body">
      <p class="feature-icon"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'environment' }) %></p>
      <h3 class="feature-title">Encrypted environment variables</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Keep secrets out of your source code. Values are encrypted at rest and injected when
        the container starts.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__body">
      <p class="feature-icon"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'domain' }) %></p>
      <h3 class="feature-title">Domains and HTTPS</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Every project gets an address immediately, served over HTTPS. Connect your own domain
        once you own one.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__body">
      <p class="feature-icon"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'overview' }) %></p>
      <h3 class="feature-title">Redeploy and roll back</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Publish an update without rebuilding your configuration, and return to a recent healthy
        release if one goes wrong.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__body">
      <p class="feature-icon"><%- include('../partials/icon', { name: 'users' }) %></p>
      <h3 class="feature-title">Team access and audit</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Invite collaborators as Owner, Maintainer, or Viewer. Deployments and configuration
        changes are recorded.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="button-group button-group--center mt-6">
  <a href="/features" class="button button--secondary">Explore All Features</a>
</div>

<div class="card mt-8">
  <div class="card__body">
    <h2 class="feature-title">What you can deploy</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">
      Static sites, Node.js and Express applications, and React projects are supported today.
      Vue and Next.js are being verified. Python, PHP, Java, and custom Dockerfiles are not
      supported yet — a runtime is only listed as supported once a full deployment has been
      tested.
    </p>
    <div class="button-group mt-4">
      <a href="/supported-runtimes" class="button button--secondary button--sm">See Supported Runtimes</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

